    frames = canvas.get("frames", []) if canvas else []
    stickies = canvas.get("stickies", []) if canvas else []

    directives = [s.get("text", "") for s in stickies if s.get("text")]
    boundaries = [f.get("title", "") for f in frames if f.get("title")]

    dir_bullets = "\n".join(f"- {d}" for d in directives[:8]) if directives else "- Enforce strict contract boundaries between UI, domain services, and persistence layers."
    bound_bullets = "\n".join(f"- {b}" for b in boundaries[:6]) if boundaries else "- UI Presentation Layer\n- Domain Services & Network\n- Data Persistence & State"

    content = f"""---
name: {skill_name}
description: Architectural directives, design contracts, and validation rules for {title} ({platform.capitalize()}). Use when implementing or reviewing {title} components and services.
---

# {title} Architecture & Quality Standard

## Mission
You are the lead systems architect and craftsmanship guardian for **{title}**.
Your role is to enforce architecture contracts, data integrity, layout precision, and quality gates when designing, generating, or modifying code for this project.

## Context & Objectives
- **Target Platform:** {platform.capitalize()}
- **Design Philosophy:** {style}
- **Concept:** {concept}

## Architectural Boundaries (Kite Topology Canvas)
{bound_bullets}

## Directives & Execution Invariants
{dir_bullets}

## Craftsmanship & UI Canons
1. **Layout Grid:** Strict 4pt (Apple HIG / macOS) and 4 epx (Windows 11 BAWA) baseline grid. Spacing values must strictly be multiples of 4 (e.g. 4, 8, 16, 24, 32).
2. **Typography & Contrast:** High contrast typography with zero muddy gray washouts. Surface cards must sit on distinct background tones.
3. **Responsive Flow:** Minimum touch/click target dimension is 44px x 44px. Smooth 120ms transitions on state changes.
4. **Zero Emojis Policy:** Decorative emojis are strictly prohibited in code, user interfaces, logs, and commit messages. Use native system icons and glyphs (SF Symbols on Apple, Segoe Fluent Icons on Windows).

## Verification Checklist
- [ ] Data layer mutations use transactions or WAL (Write-Ahead Logging).
- [ ] API endpoints enforce rate limiting and input schema validation.
- [ ] UI layouts pass accessibility tests (WCAG 2.2 AA compliant, visible focus states).
- [ ] All components preserve atomic state and recover gracefully from network disconnection.
"""

    return {
        "skill_name": skill_name,
        "content": content
    }

